cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the thermodynamic assessments and databases of the systems you use (see README.md)."
title: "Phase Diagram Explorer"
abstract: >-
  Phase Diagram Explorer computes binary temperature-composition phase diagrams
  at 1 atm from assessed CALPHAD thermodynamic databases (Compound Energy
  Formalism with Redlich-Kister excess terms and the Inden-Hillert-Jarl magnetic
  model). Equilibria come from the convex hull of the phase Gibbs energies,
  refined to exact common tangents; phase boundaries are traced adaptively and
  invariant reactions are located by root-finding. Results for the validated
  systems Ag-Cu, Pb-Sn (NIST solder database) and Fe-C (metastable Fe-Fe3C and
  stable Fe-graphite) are checked against pycalphad on the same database files,
  against the database authors' published calculations, and, for Ag-Cu and
  Fe-C, against an experimental assessment and commonly quoted textbook values.
